abstract: >-
  geoai-datacubes is an open-source Python pipeline that turns raw multi-mission
  satellite imagery into AI-ready data cubes for machine-learning and
  deep-learning workflows. From a single configuration block -- a region of
  interest, a time window, a set of bands -- it fetches, co-registers, fuses,
  and tiles imagery from 26 missions spanning direct sensor observations
  (Sentinel-2 L1C and L2A, Sentinel-1 RTC, Landsat 8/9, NAIP, PlanetScope,
  MODIS, HLS, ALOS PALSAR, Copernicus DEM, 3DEP, Sentinel-5P) and derived
  products (ESA WorldCover, JRC-GSW, ALOS-FNF, Hansen-GFC, USDA-CDL, LCMAP,
  IO-LULC, Chloris-Biomass, GEDI-L4B, GEBCO). It ships four interchangeable
  data providers (Earth Search, Microsoft Planetary Computer, Sentinel Hub,
  Planet Orders API) plus a non-STAC direct_http path for missions on
  anonymous cloud storage, a declarative per-band normalisation taxonomy,
  multi-mission fusion onto a common UTM grid, spatially-aware
  train/val/test splits, four pedagogical Colab-ready notebooks, and an
  85-test automated test suite running on GitHub Actions.
